# Fixed occurrence on integrate/phase-AI: s23's final pre-merge state (PR #629, merge
# commit 8750587b) fixed this inline check before merging -- integrate/phase-AI HEAD
# calls the canonical is_peer_receipt() accessor. s24-s30 were forked from an earlier,
# unfixed s23 commit (acaa2a43) and still carry the ad-hoc inline check forward on
# their own branches; each must merge-forward this fix independently when they merge.
<urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI23-IMPORTANT-006/integrate-8750587b>
  a triage:Occurrence ;
  triage:file "crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health/peer_delivery_router.rs" ;
  triage:line 20 ;
  triage:snippet "if message.prepared.is_peer_receipt() { // FIXED: calls canonical accessor" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closed true ;
  triage:branch "integrate/phase-AI" ;
  triage:headSha "8750587b" ;
  triage:note "AI.23 (PR #629) merged into integrate/phase-AI at 8750587b3e24c6e5a18e14315c363b6ea0f2d8e0. Independently re-verified: PostWriteRouter::dispatch now calls message.prepared.is_peer_receipt() directly instead of the ad-hoc inline check. s24-s30 occurrences remain open on their own branches (forked from a pre-fix s23 commit) and still require merge-forward." ;
  triage:occursIn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/integrate/8750587b> .

